I think lubekano3's bridi/sumti question didn't quite get answered yet;
having been new fairly recently I think I see where he's coming from. The
idea is that it makes more sense to label something in Lojban in the manner
of "This <some relation>" rather than "This is an object which <some
relation>". This is pretty much exactly what's being suggested here, with
"this" being implicit. (My explanation here may be bad, frankly; please
correct any detail mistakes).

mu'o mi'e latros.

